+#### 7.3.3.1 P25, NXDN and P25 trunking channels (multi-mode derivative)
+
+These modes have no tones, color code or contact. The record keeps their fields in those bytes; every other byte
+means what 7.3.3 says (name, frequencies, power, TOT, flags, squelch).
+
+| Offset | P25 (mode 2) | NXDN (mode 3) | P25 trunking (mode 4) |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 0x10 / 0x14 | RX / TX frequency | RX / TX frequency | Control channel / its inbound frequency |
+| 0x20 (LE16) | RX NAC 0x000-0xFFF; 0xF7E hears every NAC. Anything else (0xFFFF from an FM CPS) reads as 0xF7E | RX RAN 0-63, 0 hears every RAN; more reads as 0 | RX NAC, as P25 |
+| 0x22 (LE16) | TX NAC 0x000-0xF7D; anything else reads as 0x293 | TX RAN 0-63; more reads as 1 | The system's NAC for inbound |
+| 0x2E (LE16) | Talkgroup: TX target, and the group received | Group ID | Talkgroup for PTT |
+| 0x27-0x29, flag 1 bit 7 | Unit ID (24 bits); unset: the radio's DMR ID | Unit ID (1-65519) | Unit ID assigned by the system administrator |
+| 0x31 bit 6 | Hear every talkgroup (else ours and all call) | Hear every group | Hear every talkgroup |
+| 0x2B | RX group list (unused) | unused | Talkgroups to follow, in priority order (a list's first is the highest) |
+| 0x25, 0x2A, 0x2C, 0x2D | unused | unused | WACN bits 19-12, 11-4, 3-0 (0x2C high nibble); system ID bits 11-8 (0x2C low nibble), 7-0 (0x2D) |
+
+On a trunking channel flag 1 bit 1 (SFR) is cleared: those bytes hold the system. qdmr and the open-firmware CPS know
+modes 0 and 1 only; they keep the bytes of a record they don't edit.
+
